/-!
The relative comparison now treats old two-chains whose boundary is on the
attaching locus, not just absolute two-cycles. Componentwise simple connectivity
of the actual lifted base gives finite one-cycle fillings. A constructed lifted
downward retraction transfers these fillings to its full star. Ambient cycle
generation and unmixed old/star splitting then produce attaching two-chains
with exactly the original boundary, modulo genuine old three-boundaries.

The filling can be taken on the actual lifted attaching poset, preserving a
prescribed chain boundary there. Attaching one-boundaries are consequently
reflected from old cells. These are unconditional geometric statements for the
constructed Q universal cover over any connected base with an attaching map.

The exact Fox matrix of adjoining names is also computed. Over every receiving
group ring, zero internal coordinates mean that the old two-boundary equals the
marked word-path chain, while marked coordinates equal the name-cell coefficients.

This file is an intermediate integration point. The full theorem, including
the arbitrary CW and finite clauses, is proved by Whitehead.TheoremA in
Solution.lean.
-/
